      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's great to hear that you're feeling a bit better, but facial palsy can be a symptom of a variety of conditions, some of which may require prompt attention. While waiting a day or two might sometimes lead to improvement, there's no guarantee, and delaying medical advice could be risky if it’s the wrong condition. Most urgent care facilities also understand working schedules, so they may offer short waiting times or emergency services. Self-treatment does not substitute for professional diagnosis and it's better to get your symptoms assessed, particularly because they are still within the range that warrants medical concern. But if you decide to wait, please pay close attention to the face and watch for any other emerging symptoms—if they appear or worsen, seek medical attention immediately.",
